{"duration": 78.803, "exact_word_timing": true, "lines": [{"beat": 0, "text": "A doctor scratched cow pus into an eight-year-old boy's arm.", "start": 0.05, "end": 2.653}, {"beat": 0, "text": "The boy was James Phipps, the gardener's son.", "start": 2.733, "end": 4.819}, {"beat": 0, "text": "The doctor was Edward Jenner, in England, 1796.", "start": 4.899, "end": 7.892}, {"beat": 1, "text": "Jenner was a country doctor in Berkeley.", "start": 8.092, "end": 9.863}, {"beat": 1, "text": "Smallpox killed one in ten people around the world.", "start": 9.943, "end": 12.449}, {"beat": 1, "text": "In crowded towns, it killed one in five.", "start": 12.529, "end": 14.659}, {"beat": 1, "text": "Jenner had been inoculated for smallpox himself as a boy, and it wrecked his health for life.", "start": 14.739, "end": 18.867}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Doctors at the time used smallpox itself to protect people.", "start": 19.067, "end": 22.117}, {"beat": 2, "text": "They scratched smallpox pus into a healthy person's skin.", "start": 22.197, "end": 24.715}, {"beat": 2, "text": "That person usually got a milder case and survived.", "start": 24.795, "end": 27.299}, {"beat": 2, "text": "But sometimes they got full smallpox and died.", "start": 27.379, "end": 29.47}, {"beat": 2, "text": "And they could spread smallpox to everyone around them.", "start": 29.55, "end": 31.683}, {"beat": 3, "text": "You see, it's like fighting fire with fire, hoping the fire doesn't burn down your house.", "start": 31.883, "end": 35.778}, {"beat": 3, "text": "Jenner wanted something safer.", "start": 35.858, "end": 37.255}, {"beat": 3, "text": "He had heard that milkmaids who caught cowpox never seemed to get smallpox.", "start": 37.335, "end": 40.625}, {"beat": 3, "text": "Cowpox was a mild disease you caught from cows.", "start": 40.705, "end": 43.04}, {"beat": 4, "text": "On May fourteenth, 1796, Jenner scraped pus from cowpox blisters on the hands of Sarah Nelmes, a milkmaid.", "start": 43.24, "end": 49.379}, {"beat": 4, "text": "She had caught cowpox from a cow called Blossom.", "start": 49.459, "end": 51.613}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Jenner scratched that pus into James Phipps's arm.", "start": 51.693, "end": 53.805}, {"beat": 4, "text": "The boy got mildly sick, then recovered.", "start": 53.885, "end": 55.975}, {"beat": 5, "text": "Then Jenner did something bolder.", "start": 56.175, "end": 57.721}, {"beat": 5, "text": "He scratched actual smallpox into the boy.", "start": 57.801, "end": 59.763}, {"beat": 5, "text": "James Phipps did not get sick.", "start": 59.843, "end": 61.186}, {"beat": 5, "text": "The cowpox had protected him.", "start": 61.266, "end": 62.738}, {"beat": 6, "text": "Jenner called his method vaccination, from the Latin for cow.", "start": 62.938, "end": 65.754}, {"beat": 6, "text": "He proved it with more cases in 1798.", "start": 65.834, "end": 68.458}, {"beat": 6, "text": "The British government banned the old risky method in 1840 and gave out cowpox vaccine for free.", "start": 68.538, "end": 73.21}, {"beat": 6, "text": "The world's first vaccine was born from a milkmaid, a cow named Blossom, and a gardener's son.", "start": 73.29, "end": 77.903}], "words": [{"w": "A", "start": 0.14, "end": 0.165, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "doctor", "start": 0.19, "end": 0.39, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "scratched", "start": 0.44, "end": 0.665, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "cow", "start": 0.69, "end": 0.815, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "pus", "start": 0.865, "end": 1.065, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "into", "start": 1.09, "end": 1.24, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "an", "start": 1.265, "end": 1.34, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "eight-year-old", "start": 1.415, "end": 1.865, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "boy's", "start": 1.915, "end": 2.14, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "arm.", "start": 2.19, "end": 2.653, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "The", "start": 2.802, "end": 2.852, "line": 1, "beat": 0}, {"w": "boy", "start": 2.902, "end": 3.077, "line": 1, "beat": 0